{"id": "DfcGdJOxrYW", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why do we hang MANGO LEAVES above the door? 🌿 Your grandmother knew it was never just decoration.\n\nIt's called a toran, from the Sanskrit \"torana\": a gateway. The great stone gateways of Sanchi, over 2,000 years old, are toranas.\n\nIn the Bhagavatam, little Dhruva left home in tears. When he came back, every gate in the city had hanging mango leaves, pots of water and burning lamps (Bhagavata Purana 4.9.55). When Krishna came home to Dwarka, every door wore a festive torana (1.11.13). And the same leaves crown the kalash at every puja.\n\nSo a toran over your door says one thing: someone we love is coming home. This Diwali, that's Lakshmi. 🪔\n\nMango leaves, marigolds or beads: what's on YOUR door? Comment your state 👇\nSend this to the one who ties the toran in your home ❤️\n\n📚 Picture books of our gods, for kids: the Navadurga Set is out now. rishikatha.com (link in bio)\nFollow @therishikatha for more stories behind what we do.\n\n#toran #diwali #diwali2026 #lakshmipuja #mangoleaves #bandhanwar #hinduism #sanatandharma #bhagavatam #dhruva #krishna #indianculture #indiantraditions #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1794051863, "like_count": 2392, "comment_count": 12, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1740545403705937a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 52.899, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMf1T-qXO3X693D7EKHkYm6b0VeKG_SGv6YA1enWdguEhYVASA-JkUusXnQJQjuuMxn8T7G_ochoLqS8T-j4uSnTERgSPylBlULZ34.mp4?_nc_cat=109&_nc_oc=Adq-6cOTnCoeukhsB7SRDNMyq-xvVkJEWi0NTFzlfsN0jjJiVI4dtBrAdYOrDwxr5HAZJhu88g4aCZdGSCx79_mT&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=4eO5WgDT4GgQ7kNvwGnlhGa&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=pdZOwSHVMGFiS8VmmKl37A